cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "This citation identifies the two-step research formulation and repository. For the manuscript use paper/CITATION.bib. No numerical transport study is claimed."
type: software
title: "Recoil transport and environmental exposure of black-hole merger remnants"
authors:
  - family-names: Athota
    given-names: Venkata Hemanth
version: formulation-1
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/heyyymonth/black-hole-recoil-dynamics"
url: "https://github.com/heyyymonth/black-hole-recoil-dynamics/tree/formulation-v1"
abstract: >-
  A mathematical specification for merger-conditioned black-hole recoil transport
  and finite-time residence and environmental exposure in stellar clusters.
  Defines consistent host inputs, collisional drift and diffusion, stopping
  conventions, and a calculation handoff. No host selection, calibrated
  trajectories, or numerical outcomes are asserted for this formulation.
keywords:
  - black-hole recoil
  - stellar dynamics
  - stochastic transport
  - environmental exposure
  - reproducible research
